ty and mortality predictions for europe</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">The INTERHEART study<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b3-cia-4-319">3</xref></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12,461 cases and 14,637 controls (included in the analysis)</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Case-control</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Daily fruit and vegetable consumption</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Reduced risk of acute myocardial infarction</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">The Seven Countries Study<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b13-cia-4-319">13</xref>,<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b14-cia-4-319">14</xref></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12,763 middle-aged men</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cohort</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mediterranean-type diet</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Saturated fat is correlated with elevated incidence and morality rates of CHD</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">The SENECA Study<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b15-cia-4-319">15</xref></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">631 men and 650 women</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cohort</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diet according to healthy eating recommendations</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Decreased mortality risk</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">The HALE Study<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b16-cia-4-319">16</xref></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1,507 seemingly healthy men and 832 women</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cohort</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mediterranean diet</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Lower rate of all-causes and cause-specific mortality</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">The Framingham and offspring Study<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b17-cia-4-319">17</xref>&#x02013;<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b19-cia-4-319">19</xref></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5,124 individuals</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cohort</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diet according to healthy eating recommendations</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Positively related to other healthy lifestyle factors (smaller amount of body fat, nonsmoking and higher physical activity levels)</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mediterranean Island Study (MEDIS)<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b21-cia-4-319">21</xref></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">553 men and 637 women</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cross-sectional study</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mediterranean diet</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Greater adherence to the traditional Mediterranean diet is associated with lower cardiovascular risk</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">The Health Professional Follow-Up Study<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b26-cia-4-319">26</xref></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">42,504 men</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cohort</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Prudent-pattern diet and western-pattern diet</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Increased risk of type 2 diabetes is associated with a western-pattern diet</td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1"><bold>Clinical trials</bold></td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Indo-Mediterranean Diet Heart Study<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b27-cia-4-319">27</xref></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">499 cases and 501 controls</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Randomized controlled trial</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diet rich in whole grains, fruits, vegetables, walnuts, and almonds and a local diet similar to the step 1 National Cholesterol education Program prudent diet</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Reduction in coronary artery disease morbidity and mortality</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">The Mediterranean Diet, Cardiovascular risks and Gene Polymorphisms Study<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b28-cia-4-319">28</xref></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">102 cases and 110 controls</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Case-control study</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mediterranean type diet and low-fat diet</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Significant reduction in cardiovascular disease risk factors</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">The Lyon Diet Heart Study<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b29-cia-4-319">29</xref>,<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b30-cia-4-319">30</xref></td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">303 control subjects and 302 study subjects</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Randomized single-blind clinical trial</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mediterranean-type diet</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Reduced risk of cardiovascular complications</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-group></article>